  "action_summary": "Round 31 attacks the one property five rounds of derivation never touched: the SHAPE of the hypothesis space. Rounds 29-30 replaced every authored constant with a rule, were green, and were still answering the wrong question, because a rule inside a fixed grammar only POPULATES that grammar. Measured 2026-11-04: T_3(x)+2*T_5(x) over 19 integer points was solved COLD by storing a fifteen-entry table (18 numeric literals, 2264 bytes) and solved WARM by the identical table, even after the creature had learned both T_3 and T_5. The compositional description -- a three-entry table plus a law the creature already owned -- is eight numbers. It was not choosing the worse of two answers; it could not express the better one, because `_inline_operator_organs` only ever builds f(g(x)) and a learned law had no TERM position. That fixes the shape of every future hypothesis: Omega_t+1 = Omega_t + {compositions of what Omega_t can already express} grows in instances but never in forms. The fix adds NO new form: for each admitted unary law L, each period k the evidence supports, and op in {add,sub,mul}, the composer asks whether the residual y-L, y+L, or y/L is CONSTANT PER RESIDUE and emits T_k(x) star L(x) only when it is. The block is solved, never guessed. Result: 8 numbers instead of 18, exact on evidence, zero wrong on held-out 40..70. The change then exposed four pre-existing defects that were green for thirty rounds, all one mistake in four places: treating 'this program has nothing to say here' as 'this program says something false'. (1) derive_probe_space emitted half-steps unconditionally so an integer task was probed at x=-39.5. (2) The survivor filter read `ok and match`, so a crash eliminated a hypothesis exactly as a wrong answer did; forty survivors died at once and the creature reported CONTRADICTORY_OR_OUT_OF_GRAMMAR on a task it had solved cold. (3) synthesize_discriminating_input bucketed crashes as a distinct PREDICTION, so every half-step scored a full bit of entropy, eliminated nothing, and burned the oracle budget until it refused UNSETTLEABLE on `x mod 3`. (4) The emitted table formula silently extrapolated off the integers by taking the block of the floor, inventing a value at 2.5 that nobody claimed; a period table is a lookup by POSITION, total on the integers and silent elsewhere, and the body now raises instead of inventing. Safety is unchanged and both halves are asserted: a total program returning a wrong value still dies at the probe, and a partial one must still survive every probe it can answer plus all of the evidence. Also corrected, honestly: my comparison harness silently taught nothing for several hours (both teaching calls returned UNSETTLEABLE and organs_in_stratum was empty, so the composer was handed zero laws and produced zero candidates), which is round 30's 'a silent no-op is indistinguishable from a wrong answer' arriving in a new place -- the test file now asserts the premise before the conclusion. Two suites I had believed pre-existing were traced to my own round 26 and both were asserting OLDER, WORSE behaviour: an exactly-determined three-point affine must NOT be called corroborated (round 26's own rule), and `x*x` must NOT be refused when the weight-1 identity times x reproduces it exactly; both assertions were corrected, and I got the affine law's arithmetic wrong once in the process and the creature was right. Round 30's measured polynomial degree also made `x^3` expressible as a law, so a round-26 test whose premise was 'x^3 is outside this grammar' is now obsolete and was replaced with a genuine recitation, plus the converse assertion that a cubic IS testable.",
